# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ArcadeVaultV6 — SVP Chain Testnet (chain id 2517)
#
# The app calls ArcadeVaultV6 and VynarRewardsV3. There is no V5 variable any more:
# renaming these is the whole point of the migration, and leaving a V5 name here would
# mean getServerEnv() throws on first call instead of failing visibly at boot.
#
# HISTORY, because this file has lied before: it documented ArcadeVaultV3 and a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VYNAR_DISTRIBUTOR_ADDRESS that no code reads, and it documented the
# distributor as V2 when the code read ..._REWARDS_V2_ADDRESS. Copying it verbatim silently
# disabled the entire VYR reward surface. If a name here does not match a `process.env`
# read in lib/, believe the code and fix this file.
#
# Contracts/ArcadeVaultV2.sol, VynarDistributor.sol and Vynar.sol are superseded and are NOT
# what runs. The Solidity source of V6/V3/StakingVault lives OUTSIDE this repo; only the ABIs
# (lib/arcade-vault-v6-abi.ts, lib/vynar-rewards-v3-abi.ts) are here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Exposed to the browser. Same address as the server variable below.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ARCADE_VAULT_V6_ADDRESS=0x...
# Server-only copy. The app is on V6; there is no V5 variable any more.
ARCADE_VAULT_V6_ADDRESS=0x...

# Chain. CHAIN_ID must be exactly 2517 and REQUIRED_PAYMENT_AMOUNT exactly 0.1;
# getServerEnv() throws on first call if either differs, which fails the whole app.
#
# REQUIRED_PAYMENT_AMOUNT only governs the price ADVERTISED for the `human` mode, and
# getServerEnv() checks it against HUMAN_ENTRY_FEE in lib/arcade-arenas.ts. The amount actually
# charged is revalidated against the on-chain fee of whichever arena was requested, in
# verifyPayment(). Modes are priced 0.1 / 0.5 / 1.0 SVP and all of them live in that registry,
# so there is no variable per arena and adding one would reintroduce the duplication that made
# AGENT move from id 1 to 3 without anyone noticing.
CHAIN_ID=2517
REQUIRED_PAYMENT_AMOUNT=0.1

# RPC failover. SVP_RPC_URLS wins; RPC_URL is the single-endpoint fallback.
SVP_RPC_URLS=https://svp-dataseed1-testnet.svpchain.org,https://svp-dataseed2-testnet.svpchain.org,https://svp-dataseed3-testnet.svpchain.org
RPC_URL=https://svp-dataseed1-testnet.svpchain.org
RPC_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
RPC_COOLDOWN_MS=15000
RPC_FAILURE_THRESHOLD=3
RPC_DEADLINE_MS=12000

# Epoch duration is derived from the environment name, NOT from a numeric variable.
# AUDIT FIX: the old ARCADE_EPOCH_DURATION=3600 here was read by nothing. Duration is
# 86400s in production and 1200s otherwise, and the contract snapshots it per epoch.
#
# AUDIT FIX: APP_ENV and NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV both select the duration and MUST agree.
# Setting only one leaves the client and the server computing different epochs.
# Set both to 'production' together, or to anything else together.
APP_ENV=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=production
# Optional. Overrides the leaderboard page's auto-refresh interval (seconds).
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEADERBOARD_REFRESH_SECONDS=15

# ────────────────────────────────────────���────────────────────────────────────
# VynarRewardsV3 — rewards distributor and VYNAR token
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_VYNAR_ADDRESS=0xf9eE728B5D1829B99693C3551048c06239d37ff2
# The name the code reads is VYNAR_REWARDS_V3_ADDRESS, in lib/vynar-config.ts. It has been
# documented here under three different names (DISTRIBUTOR, REWARDS_V2, now V3) and every
# mismatch disabled all VYR rewards silently, so check lib/vynar-config.ts before trusting
# this file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VYNAR_REWARDS_V3_ADDRESS=0x...
NEXT_PUBLIC_VYNAR_CHAIN_ID=2517
# Server-only fallback, read by lib/vynar-rewards-v3-abi.ts when the NEXT_PUBLIC_ name is absent.
# Server code must never take the address from the public variable: a browser-visible value is
# not a trust boundary, and the signing server would be trusting an env var a client can observe.
VYNAR_REWARDS_V3_ADDRESS=0x...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# StakingVault — SVP + VYNAR staking, 1-day lock
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ETAPA 6 (pendiente): el ABI y el contrato ya existen (lib/staking-vault-abi.ts), pero TODA la
# app que los consume viene en esa etapa. No hay todavia ninguna ruta que balancee o retire, asi
# que dejar esto vacio no rompe nada; rellenarlo antes si se despliega el contrato.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STAKING_VAULT_ADDRESS=0x...
# Server-only fallback, same shape as the vault pair above.
STAKING_VAULT_ADDRESS=0x...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Publishable (anon) key. Only used where a public read is genuinely anonymous;
# arcade_scores is no longer readable this way, the narrow arcade_leaderboard_public
# view is.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Legacy alias, read as a fallback for the two above.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only. service_role bypasses RLS; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server secrets
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Private key of the gameServerSigner, used to EIP-712 sign recordScore().
# SOLO servidor: nunca usar NEXT_PUBLIC_ ni exponerla al cliente.
GAME_SERVER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Gates /api/cron/* and /api/incentive/publish.
CRON_SECRET=

# HMAC key for the wallet sign-in session cookie (lib/wallet-auth.ts). Must be at
# least 32 characters. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
# Without it every wallet-scoped endpoint fails closed with AUTH_UNAVAILABLE.
WALLET_AUTH_SECRET=